# CR 103.1-103.4: DealOpeningHands shuffles each library and deals seven
# cards before any mulligan decision exists to make -- distinct from
# PerformMulligans below, which only runs the London mulligan procedure on
# whatever DealOpeningHands already dealt, and takes no coin flip of its
# own. queue startingplayer answers ChooseStartingPlayer's own CR 103.2
# coin flip; the answer does not depend on which player g.rand happened to
# ask, so naming human here is deterministic regardless of the flip itself,
# and ten identical Mountains per library makes the shuffle's own
# randomness unobservable too. Both players keep their opening hand -- no
# mulligan happens at all.
queue startingplayer human
dealopeninghands
queue keephand true
queue keephand true
mulligan human
